Stdout:
ST403  Mass assignment
checks mass_assignment

Write stored a field that clients must not set, such as a `readOnly` or
privilege field.

  POST  /users     201  {"id": 7, "name": "a", "role": "user"}
  POST  /users     201  {"id": 8, "name": "a", "role": "admin"}   # sent with "role": "admin"
  GET   /users/8   200  {"id": 8, "name": "a", "role": "admin"}

Bind request bodies to an allowlist of writable fields, and ignore or reject the
rest with `400` or `422`. A field clients may set belongs in the request schema
without `readOnly`. The check is off unless enabled:

  # schemathesis.toml
  [checks]
  mass_assignment.enabled = true

`--exclude-checks mass_assignment` turns it off.
